MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WHY
Article 14 of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847 has applied since 11 September 2026
and, by Art. 69(3), applies to every in-scope product placed on the market
before 11 December 2027 — no grandfathering, and the duty outlives the support
period. It is the only CRA obligation that is live today, it carries a 24-hour
clock, and the fine ceiling is EUR 15m or 2.5% of worldwide turnover. Nothing
in this repository could answer "when did you know, and can you show me".

WHAT
A new `assurance/` package with no runtime dependencies and no import of
`palletizer_full`:

  core/       content addressing, the EvidenceObject protocol, assurance tiers
  evidence/   append-only hash-chained ledger (SQLite)
  security/   art14: domain model, deadline clock, triage, the 39-field ENISA
              platform specification, case engine, reports, CLI

Three things it does that a checklist cannot:

  * Records the awareness moment independently. The platform does not yet
    capture it for vulnerabilities and records *detection* for incidents; this
    register is the compensating control and requires the reasoning with it.
  * Computes both final-report clocks correctly. A vulnerability report is due
    14 days after a corrective OR MITIGATING measure becomes available; an
    incident report one month after the 72-hour notification was SUBMITTED.
  * Surfaces the platform's counter defect (ENISA FAQ 26 — the 72-hour counter
    displays 48 hours after the early warning) instead of silently disagreeing
    with it.

CUSTOMER VALUE
This is the deliverable of the first paid engagement, as software rather than
templates: a manufacturer runs it, and the artifacts it produces are the
evidence. Repeat delivery is configuration, not consulting.

RISK
Additive. No existing module is modified; the only change outside the new tree
is two lines in pyproject.toml (package discovery and the `assurance` console
script).

ROLLBACK
git revert of this commit. Nothing imports the new tree.

TESTS
114 new tests, 94% coverage of the new package, ruff clean. Full suite:
1104 passed, 14 skipped (was 990 passed, 14 skipped).

Includes an 8-thread concurrency test proving the ledger cannot fork under
parallel writers, and tamper tests for edited, removed and re-ordered records.
Deadline tests assert against the article, not the implementation.

SUCCESS CONDITION
A case can be carried from first signal to filed early warning through the CLI,
the chain verifies, and the export refuses if it does not. Met.

